+### Follow-up coverage
+
+Three areas that the review listed as unverified now have automated checks:
+
+- Missing assertions in a nested leaf section, exhausted and fail-then-pass,
+  for the recorder, JUnit, SonarQube, TeamCity, and TAP. The new checks found
+  two defects, both fixed: TAP repeated the `Attempt k of M failed:` heading
+  for every diagnostic of a superseded attempt instead of writing it once,
+  and JUnit and SonarQube labelled a missing-assertion failure in a section
+  as `no assertions in test case`; they now say `no assertions in section`.
+- The fatal-error path for every built-in reporter. Console, compact, TAP,
+  TeamCity, SonarQube, and Automake output is identical with and without
+  `--retry-failed 2`; JSON differs only by the attempt keys; XML parses and
+  contains one final attempt; JUnit parses and counts the fatal error once.
+- `--break` with retries, through `RetryFailed::DebugBreak`. The binary is
+  built from the amalgamated sources with a recording
+  `CATCH_BREAK_INTO_DEBUGGER`, because the break happens inside the library.
+  Every failed assertion breaks, including those of superseded attempts, and
+  the break happens inside its attempt.
+
+`RetryFailed::Fatal` now runs serially, waits up to 120 seconds for each
+crashing child instead of 20, and prints how long each child took. Its single
+earlier timeout on Windows was not reproduced and its cause is unknown.
+
+The amalgamated sources were regenerated with
+`python3 tools/scripts/generateAmalgamatedFiles.py` on Linux, where the
+changes were first built with GCC in a development build (`basic-tests` 91/91;
+`RetryFailed::Scenarios`, `RetryFailed::Fatal`, `RetryFailed::DebugBreak`,
+and `AmalgamatedFileTest` 4/4). The changes were then validated on Windows
+with the existing incremental build trees:
+
+```powershell
+cmake -B C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\basic-test-build -S . -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug --preset basic-tests
+cmake --build C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\basic-test-build --config Debug --parallel
+ctest --test-dir C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\basic-test-build -C Debug --output-on-failure -R 'RunTests|ApprovalTests'
+ctest --test-dir C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\basic-test-build -C Debug --output-on-failure
+cmake -B C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\debug-build -S . -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug --preset all-tests
+cmake --build C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\debug-build --config Debug --parallel
+ctest --test-dir C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\debug-build -C Debug --output-on-failure -R 'RetryFailed::|AmalgamatedFileTest|ApprovalTests'
+ctest --test-dir C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\debug-build -C Debug --output-on-failure -j 4
+ctest --test-dir C:\build\Course_AI\catch2\debug-build -C Debug -R 'RetryFailed::Fatal' --repeat until-fail:10 --output-on-failure
+```
+
+Results: `basic-tests` 92/92 and focused 2/2 with no build warnings;
+`all-tests` 158/158 (157 earlier tests plus `RetryFailed::DebugBreak`) and
+focused 15/15, with only the four baseline `D9025` warnings; no
+`*.unapproved.txt` files. `RetryFailed::Fatal` passed 10 of 10 repeated runs,
+taking 43 to 63 seconds for its 18 crashing children. On Linux the same test
+takes under a second, which suggests that most of the Windows time is spent
+in the operating system's crash handling.
+
