+With retries disabled, reporter output is unchanged. With retries enabled,
+these representations apply even to a test case that runs only once:
+
+* XML and JSON add structural attempt information.
+* JUnit's suite `tests`, `failures`, `errors`, and `skipped` attributes count
+  logical test cases instead of assertions, so a test case with several
+  assertions counts once and a fatal error counts as an error.
+* Accepted failures (`[!mayfail]` or an expected failure under
+  `[!shouldfail]`) are represented as skipped in JUnit and marked `TODO` in
+  TAP.
+* JUnit, SonarQube, TeamCity, and TAP report failures that have no failed
+  assertion, such as a test case or leaf section without assertions under
+  `-w NoAssertions`, or an unexpected pass under `[!shouldfail]`, as failures
+  with their reason.
+
+TAP buffers its own lines until an attempt ends, so those lines can
 interleave differently with output written directly by the test.
 
